# hyperlaunch config. Hyperlaunch.app edits this file for you; you can also edit it
# by hand. Changes apply as soon as you save. To check it: ~/.local/bin/hyperlaunch --check
#
# Keys
#   hyperkey <key> = <modifiers>   hold the key and other keys get these modifiers
#                                  (cmd ctrl opt shift: all four make a full Hyper key)
#   remap <key> = <modifiers> <key>  pressing the key presses this shortcut instead
#   <key> can also be capslock, mic, spotlight or dnd (the top-row keys on recent
#   Apple keyboards), or codeN for any other key code.
#
# App shortcuts (Hyper + key)
#   <key> = <app>   the app is a full path, or just its name (anything `open -a` accepts)
#   key names: a-z, 0-9, f1-f12, space, return, tab, escape, delete, left, right, up,
#   down, or one of  - [ ] ; ' , . / \ `   (write "equal" for the = key)
#
# when-in-front: what an app shortcut does when its app is already in front.
#   minimize (minimize its windows), hide (like Cmd+H), or nothing (just bring it forward).
#   Pressing the shortcut again brings the app back.

hyperkey capslock = ctrl opt shift cmd
# remap mic = opt space

when-in-front = minimize

b = Safari
e = /System/Library/CoreServices/Finder.app
t = Terminal
n = Notes
s = System Settings
, = ~/Applications/Hyperlaunch.app
